## Text

The rules below cover plain text and lightweight markup such as Markdown; structured formats (e.g. JSON, YAML) follow their own format instead.

### Formats

- Write each paragraph on one line; never hard-wrap mid-sentence, unless the file targets a fixed-width form (e.g. a plain-text changelog or license notice), then hard-wrap the whole file at one width between 72 and 79 columns.
- Use ASCII punctuation and straight quotes by default; use non-ASCII characters only where the content requires them (names, quoted text, symbols with no ASCII form, box-drawing in layout trees).
- End every file with a single final newline; strip trailing blank lines.
- Separate headings from body text with exactly one blank line; never indent paragraphs or headings except intentional block quotes.
